{"name":"Dapple Grey","hex":"#959486","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dapple grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of dapple-grey, UK standard spelling of dapple-gray"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of dapple-grey, UK standard spelling of dapple-gray"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dapple_grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gray horse","blocks":[{"text":"A gray horse has a coat color characterized by progressive depigmentation of the colored hairs of the coat. Most gray horses have black skin and dark eyes; unlike some equine dilution genes and some other genes that lead to depigmentation, gray does not affect skin or eye color. Gray horses may be born any base color, depending on other color genes present. White hairs begin to appear at or shortly after birth and become progressively more prevalent as the horse ages as white hairs become intermingled with hairs of other colors. Graying can occur at different rates—very quickly on one horse and very slowly on another. As adults, most gray horses eventually become completely white, though some retain intermixed light and dark hairs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Lipizzaner_DSC02439.jpg/330px-Lipizzaner_DSC02439.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_horse"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Stutemitfohlen.jpg/330px-Stutemitfohlen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Stutemitfohlen.jpg/330px-Stutemitfohlen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A gray mare with suckling foal. The mare has a white hair coat, but the underlying black skin confirms that she is gray and not white. The light hairs around the foal's muzzle and eyes indicate that it will gray like its mother. Not all foals show signs of graying this young.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStutemitfohlen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Arabian_Simeon_Stud%284428278721%29.jpg/500px-Arabian_Simeon_Stud%284428278721%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Arabian_Simeon_Stud%284428278721%29.jpg/500px-Arabian_Simeon_Stud%284428278721%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArabian_Simeon_Stud(4428278721).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg/500px-Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg/1280px-Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg/500px-Irish_Sport_Horse_-_Assagart_Lord_Lancer_standing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki